  "question": {
    "text": "If the function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>g</mo><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>{</mo><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>k</mi><msqrt><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></msqrt><mtext>&#160;&#160;,&#160;&#160;</mtext></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2&#160;&#160;</mn><mtext>,&#160;&#160;</mtext></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;is differentiable, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi></math> is&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
